      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T17:05:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, then at least `lib2` is going to need to pass something in to indicate how to do text shaping, in the same way it\u0027s going to need to pass in a `ResourceProvider`. In fact, maybe it would be better to add all of this to `ResourceProvider` instead? (Or something like it, which is essentially that this CL currently is.) In addition to loading named assets we need a way to provide text shaping implementations.\n\nAlso G3 gets away with many sins, as no one there writes libraries. Which is also why Skia hasn\u0027t been a library (it\u0027s just a source dump of application code that one can compile into an application).",
      "parentUuid": "552e5b1d_573bacfb",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a463aa8_c8b2ba24",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T18:11:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It\u0027s not the top level app that needs to make this decision - it\u0027s whomever is depending directly on skottie, specifically whomever creates the animation.\n\nHaving a library bound to a particular configuration sounds extremely limiting.\n\n```\ncc_binary(\n    name \u003d \"app1\",\n    deps \u003d [\":lib1\"],\n)\n\ncc_binary(\n    name \u003d \"app2\",\n    deps \u003d [\":lib1\"],\n)\n```\n\n`app1` runs on iOS and wants coretext shaping, `app2` runs on android and wants harfbuzz.  They both rely on Lottie templating logic implemented in `lib1`.",
      "parentUuid": "d9b15540_087d3a83",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6454b43a_8b164053",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T18:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Well, then at least lib2 is going to need to pass something in to indicate how to do text shaping, in the same way it\u0027s going to need to pass in a ResourceProvider.\n\nThe difference I see is ResourceProvider is an interface, designed to be implemented by the client, whereas the text shaping callbacks are just selectors for something we implement internally.\n\n\u003e In fact, maybe it would be better to add all of this to ResourceProvider instead?\n\nGood thought, if we are to pass explicit factories, that may be the least disruptive way to go about it.",
      "parentUuid": "6a463aa8_c8b2ba24",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a30f6c1_a403404e",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-28T21:26:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, SkShaper and SkUnicode are also just interfaces, for which we implement a few common implementations that can be used, just like ResourceProvider. These aren\u0027t just selectors, any more than SkFontMgr is \"just a selector\".",
      "parentUuid": "6454b43a_8b164053",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69b5a739_ab9b5b28",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T13:59:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can look at how these are being extended in practice.\n\nThe Skia ResourceProvider implementations are either used internally for our tools or are utilities to wrap other client provided RPs.  Any client that cares about asset management is going to provide their own implementation.  I counted at least 8 client impls.\n\nSkFontMgr is being extended by some sophisticated clients, but also most instances require some client-provided configuration information.\n\nThe only purpose of SkShaper and SkUnicode in SVG/Skottie APIs is to select one of Skia\u0027s impls.  Would we still consider this approach if the same was achievable at the build system level?",
      "parentUuid": "7a30f6c1_a403404e",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7dbfbbf6_f517515a",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T14:21:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`modules/skshaper/utils/FactoryHelpers.h` exists purely for convenience, anyone could implement an `SkShapers::Factory` with whatever the want.\n\nSVG/Skottie can of course just select one of Skia\u0027s impls if they want, but that means that they need to depend on them directly. So yes, this is achievable at the build system level if SVG/Skottie  are willing to depend on one of Skia\u0027s impls directly.",
      "parentUuid": "69b5a739_ab9b5b28",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7edaa041_ce43fcfe",
        "filename": "modules/skshaper/src/SkShaper_factory.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 20
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T14:44:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hard-coding the configuration at the intermediate library level is not useful.  Why can\u0027t that be delegated to clients?\n\n```\ncc_binary(\n    name \u003d \"app\",\n    deps \u003d [\n       \":skia_svg\",\n       \":skia_shaper_harfbuzz_impl\",\n       \":skia_unicode_icu_impl\",\n       ...\n    ],\n)\n```",
      "parentUuid": "7dbfbbf6_f517515a",
      "revId": "464553d57f1f451ac3853d91b3a079749175c00f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
